PostgreSQL Upgrade - pg_utility
==================================

1. verify how much free space in FS (if using --copy mode)
2. initdb NEW CLUSTER
   - Use the same checksum setting as the old cluster.
   - (For PG18 and 18+, data checksums are enabled by default during initdb, HENCE use "initdb --no-data-checksums" if the old cluster has checksums disabled.)
3. pg_upgrade --checks (+ --link checks if needed)
4. take backup of OLD cluster conf files
5. compare and prepare conf files for NEW MAJOR VERSION OF PG
6. copy prepared conf files to new PG cluster
7. start new cluster (on different port if needed like 5433) and verify it starts correctly and check logs and stop new cluster
8. run again: pg_upgrade --checks (+ --link checks if needed)
9. run actual upgrade: pg_upgrade (--copy or --link)
	|_ WARNING: If the NEW cluster is still off after upgrade, DO NOT START with systemctl as it will be having OLD DATADIR location set.
				This is very dangerous for --link mode as it will corrupt the PG data files due to hard links. Use $NEW_PG_BIN/pg_ctl instead to start new cluster.
	|_ Validate pg_upgrade logs as well.
10. Run on NEW CLUSTER: vacuumdb --analyze-in-stages (or the analyze script generated by pg_upgrade).
11. delete old cluster
	|_ if upgraded with --copy mode: you can keep old cluster for 1-2 day in case of rollback
	|_ if upgraded with --link mode: dont START old cluster even by mistake as the old cluster is NOT-USABLE anymore after upgrade and due to hard links it can corrupt new cluster if old cluster started, so delete the OLD CLUSTER on the spot after successful upgrade verification.
12. pg_ctl stop ---- new cluster
		|_ + reset the port to old value (if you changed it in earlier steps)
13. Update DATADIR in systemctl to NEW CLUSTER.
14. Start new cluster with systemctl. Verify logs.
15. Deliver database to App team.
16. Take full DB backup of up new cluster (from commvault or other backup tool)
		|_ if you have time, the backup step can be done before delivering the database to APP team.

------------- Finish -------------------

